    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110622" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φή </span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῆ</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Aristarch.
		</span></i>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς</span>
			, <i>as, like as,</i> read by Zenodotus in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.144
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				14.499
			</span></i>, said by Sch.A on <i><span class="en">
				14.499
			</span></i> to occur in <i><span class="en">
				Antim.
			</span></i> (he cites <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				79
			</span></i>) and in <i><span class="en">
				Call.
			</span></i> (v. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Frr.</u>
				366
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				518
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φή ῥα</span> prob. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δή ῥα</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῆρα</span>
			) in <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				241
			</span></i>.</div>
